>> title: Chicken Tikka
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, indian, yogurt, grill, starter
>> counters: Curry House, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: murgh tikka, tikka, chicken tikka kebab, tandoori chicken tikka
>> pairs-with: tandoori-marinade, mint-chutney, kachumber
>> servings: 6
>> time: 7 hr
>> slack: narrow — the fourteen minutes is a race between the crust setting and the thigh drying out, and a home grill loses it slowly
>> washing-up: a bowl to marinate in, the metal skewers, the broiler tray

>> step: slash and marinate 6 hr
Marinate @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; cut in 2-in pieces and slashed to the middle) in @tandoori marinade{1 1/2%cup}(360 g; the marinade recipe) ~marinate{6%hr}, covered, in the fridge.

>> step: thread on skewers, alternating
Thread @&(~1)marinated chicken{} onto metal #skewers{} with @red onion{1}(cut in 1-in squares, layers separated) and @green bell pepper{1}(in 1-in squares), leaving a finger's gap between the pieces so the heat gets all the way round.

>> step: grill 14 min, turning, until the edges blacken
Grill @&(~1)skewers{} over the hottest charcoal, or under a #broiler{} on the top rung, ~grill{14%min}, turning often, until the marinade sets to a dry crust and the edges blacken.

>> step: brush and dust, off the heat
Brush @melted ghee{2%Tbs}(28 g) over @&(~1)cooked tikka{} and dust it with @chaat masala{1/2%tsp} and @lemon juice{1%Tbs}(15 mL) off the heat.

A home grill is half a tandoor's heat so keep it close with thigh rather than breast and heat rather than patience.
